-# FriendProgressFeed
-FriendProgressFeed OSRS plugin+# Friend Progress Feed
+
+Friend Progress Feed is a RuneLite external plugin that posts a small in-game progress feed while you play. The current implementation tracks visible progress for the local player and is structured so friend/clan feed sources can be added later without changing the plugin metadata or package layout.
+
+## What it does
+
+- Shows an optional login confirmation once RuneLite reaches `LOGGED_IN`.
+- Tracks stat changes from RuneLite's `StatChanged` event.
+- Announces level-ups by default.
+- Can announce large XP drops when enabled in config.
+- Formats all messages with a `[Friend Progress]` prefix so they are easy to spot in the game chat.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Open RuneLite's plugin configuration panel and search for `Friend Progress Feed`.
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Announce level-ups | On | Posts a feed message when the tracked account gains a level. |
+| Announce XP drops | Off | Posts XP-gain feed messages when the XP threshold is met. |
+| Minimum XP drop | 10,000 | Minimum XP gained in a single stat update before an XP-drop message is posted. |
+| Show login message | On | Confirms that the plugin is tracking after login. |
+
+## Build and test
+
+Use Java 11, matching RuneLite/plugin-hub expectations:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+To launch a developer client from this repo:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew run --no-daemon
+```
+
+## Repository layout
+
+- `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/friendprogressfeed/FriendProgressFeedPlugin.java` - RuneLite plugin entry point and event handlers.
+- `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/friendprogressfeed/FriendProgressFeedConfig.java` - RuneLite config items.
+- `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/friendprogressfeed/FriendProgressFeedFormatter.java` - small pure-Java formatting and threshold helpers.
+- `src/test/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/friendprogressfeed/FriendProgressFeedPluginTest.java` - lightweight unit tests that do not require a live RuneLite client.
+- `src/test/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/friendprogressfeed/FriendProgressFeedPluginTestClient.java` - developer-mode launch harness used by the Gradle `run` task.
+- `runelite-plugin.properties` - RuneLite external plugin metadata.
+
+## API usage notes
+
+This version does not call Wise Old Man, TempleOSRS, or any other external API. It relies only on RuneLite client events, so it has no network credentials, rate limits, or API failure states.
+
+Future friend/clan progress aggregation should use a background executor, cache API responses, and surface API failures quietly so the game thread is never blocked.
+
+## Manual RuneLite testing checklist
+
+1. Launch with `./gradlew run --no-daemon` using Java 11.
+2. Confirm `Friend Progress Feed` appears in the plugin list with the display name, description, tags, and config items from this repo.
+3. Log into OSRS and verify the optional `[Friend Progress] ... tracking ...` chat line appears once.
+4. Gain a level and confirm a level-up feed message appears.
+5. Enable `Announce XP drops`, lower `Minimum XP drop` if desired, gain XP, and confirm XP-drop messages respect the threshold.
+6. Toggle each config option and verify the chat feed behavior changes without restarting RuneLite.
+
+## Plugin-hub prep
+
+Before plugin-hub submission, capture a screenshot or GIF of the chat feed during manual testing and revisit whether friend/clan API-backed progress aggregation should be included in v1 or documented as follow-up work.
